          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 239,
              "body": "Ideally \"members\" can be expanded to IP or routeSet Object class but members attributes also supports  below syntax \n\n\"members: 5.0.0.0/8^+, 30.0.0.0/8^24-32, rs-foo^+\" which will be difficult to expand.\n\nMay be we can put RIR search object for such cases. What do you  guys think? Should we keep it as list of strings for simplicity ? ",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T11:56:04Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T12:05:39Z"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOQa7tLM7Qnkdj",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "0afaf76"
          },
          "author": "maggarwal13",
          "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "body": "",
          "createdAt": "2025-11-24T11:57:10Z",
          "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T11:57:10Z",
          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 287,
              "body": "\"members\" here can easily be expanded to autnum and asSet object class, but for consistency with routeSet I decided to go with  array of strings",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T11:57:10Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T12:05:57Z"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOQa7tLM7QnoHo",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "0afaf76"
          },
          "author": "maggarwal13",
          "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "body": "",
          "createdAt": "2025-11-24T12:01:54Z",
          "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T12:01:54Z",
          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 510,
              "body": "For this change I took a hint from Andy's work [route-policy](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-newton-weirds-route-policy-00) But there he mentions order of objects needs to be preserved but as per my understanding of rfc2280#section-6.1 ordering might not be necessary.",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T12:01:54Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T12:01:54Z"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOQa7tLM7QpTqZ",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "665d301"
          },
          "author": "anewton1998",
          "authorAssociation": "NONE",
          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "body": "Good start.\r\n\r\nI left comments about using the extension Id and link relationships that would apply to most of the object classes.",
          "createdAt": "2025-11-24T13:51:30Z",
          "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T14:05:16Z",
          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 5,
              "body": "Extension is the common term used instead of support.",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T13:51:30Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T14:05:16Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 9,
              "body": "if you change it to \"extension\" be sure to change this as well.\r\n\r\nBTW, no need to change the repo name.",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T13:52:31Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T14:05:16Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 34,
              "body": "regext",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T13:53:02Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T14:05:16Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 36,
              "body": "regext@ietf.org",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T13:53:13Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T14:05:16Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 56,
              "body": "ICANN",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T13:53:31Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T14:05:16Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 527,
              "body": "I would shorten the extension id to \"irr\" or \"irr0\". The RDAP part is given, and RDAP extensions that include opaque major versioning tend to start with 0 instead of 1 (that's not a rule though).",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T13:56:58Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T14:05:16Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 110,
              "body": "Each of these needs to be prefixed with the extension id, such as \"irrRdap1_route\". See my comment about using \"irr0\".",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T13:57:57Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T14:05:16Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 137,
              "body": "object class names also need to be prefixed with the extension Id: \"irr0_route\".",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T13:58:38Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T14:05:16Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 187,
              "body": "Expanding on this could be useful. A link to an RDAP autnum object and network object would be good. And for this reason, we should think about defining relationships, such as \"rdap_irr0_autnum\" and \"rdap_irr0_ipNetwork\". Thoughts?",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T14:01:03Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T14:05:16Z"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOQa7tLM7QrApe",
          "commit": {
