          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 110,
              "body": "Well we do not prefix extension_id for any other path segments, so to be consistent may be we should not ?  I remember a discussion about  an extension RFC , are you suggesting this change w.r.t to that ? ",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T15:26:18Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T15:27:24Z"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOQa7tLM7QrSza",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "665d301"
          },
          "author": "maggarwal13",
          "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "body": "",
          "createdAt": "2025-11-24T15:31:36Z",
          "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T15:31:36Z",
          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 187,
              "body": "Each object returned will have a self link as per  RFC9083#Section 4.2. Something like this :\r\n\r\n  \"links\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"value\": \"https://example.net/route/193.254.30.0/24AS1272\",\r\n      \"rel\": \"self\",\r\n      \"href\": \"https://example.net/route/193.254.30.0/24AS1272\",\r\n      \"type\": \"application/rdap+json\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n\r\nand for route object \"origin\" and \"prefix\"  will also have a self link too. May be I should paste whole example so it would be clearer.  What do you think?  ",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-24T15:31:36Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-24T15:31:37Z"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOQa7tLM7Qt8Js",
